# Gemini 2 Body Tracking in Godot

## Goal

Implement robust real-time body tracking in Godot using:

- Godot 4.x
- Orbbec Gemini 2
- Orbbec SDK v2
- MediaPipe Pose Landmarker
- GDMP for MediaPipe integration with Godot
- Gemini 2 depth data for accurate 3D joint positions

The final system must expose clean, game-oriented body tracking data to GDScript.

The game code should not need to know anything about MediaPipe, Orbbec SDK, image alignment, camera intrinsics, or depth sampling.

The desired high-level API should look approximately like:

```gdscript
var player := BodyTracker.get_player(0)

var hand := player.right_hand

print(hand.position_3d)
print(hand.velocity)
print(hand.confidence)

if player.is_crouching:
    pass

if player.gestures.has("push"):
    cast_spell()
```

Do not build the actual game yet.

Build the reusable tracking layer first.

---

# 1. Architecture

Use this architecture:

```text
                 Orbbec Gemini 2
                       │
               Orbbec SDK v2
                       │
             synchronized FrameSet
                ┌──────┴───────┐
                │              │
              RGB            Depth
                │              │
                │        D2C alignment
                │              │
                ▼              │
       MediaPipe Pose          │
          Landmarker           │
                │              │
          33 landmarks         │
            in RGB XY          │
                │              │
                └──────┬───────┘
                       │
               sample depth
              around each joint
                       │
               camera intrinsics
                       │
                 deprojection
                       │
                       ▼
                true XYZ joints
                       │
                   smoothing
                       │
                  player IDs
                       │
                  velocities
                       │
                       ▼
                  BodyTracker
                       │
             ┌─────────┼──────────┐
             ▼         ▼          ▼
          gestures   game      particles/VFX
```

Important:

**Do not use MediaPipe's Z coordinate as the authoritative physical depth.**

Use MediaPipe primarily for joint detection in image space.

Use the Gemini 2 depth sensor to obtain physical Z and deproject the joints into camera-space XYZ coordinates.

