# 15. Persistent Player IDs

MediaPipe detections should not be assumed to maintain permanent player identity.

For two-player games, implement your own identity tracker.

Start simple.

Calculate each person's body center from something like:

```text
midpoint(left_hip, right_hip)
```

Match new detections against previous players based on nearest body-center location.

Use a sensible maximum movement distance.

Maintain:

```text
Player 1
Player 2
```

even when MediaPipe returns detections in a different order.

Later improve identity matching using:

```text
position
velocity
body dimensions
tracking history
```

Do not use face recognition.

---

# 16. Crossing Players

Test explicitly:

```text
Player A starts left
Player B starts right

A walks past B

A ends on right
B ends on left
```

Their IDs should ideally remain stable.

If perfect crossing behavior becomes disproportionately complicated, prioritize:

```text
stable normal gameplay
```

over sophisticated re-identification.

Document limitations.

---

# 17. Body Center

Calculate a useful body root.

Prefer something like:

```text
hips_center =
    (left_hip + right_hip) / 2
```

Optionally calculate:

```text
shoulder_center
torso_center
```

Expose:

```gdscript
player.position
```

as the chosen body root.

