# 28. Testing

Implement at least these manual scenarios.

### Test 1 — standing still

One person stands approximately 2 metres from the camera.

Verify:

- skeleton stable
- depth approximately correct
- low jitter

### Test 2 — hand forward

Move right hand toward camera.

Verify:

```text
Z changes substantially
```

while torso depth remains relatively stable.

This proves Gemini depth fusion is working.

### Test 3 — sideways movement

Walk left/right.

Verify X changes correctly.

### Test 4 — crouch

Verify hip/knee positions respond correctly.

### Test 5 — jump

Verify body-root vertical velocity.

### Test 6 — two players

Both people visible simultaneously.

Verify two skeletons.

### Test 7 — player crossing

Walk past one another.

Inspect whether IDs remain stable.

### Test 8 — occlusion

Hide one hand behind the torso.

The tracker should degrade gracefully instead of producing wild XYZ coordinates.

