# 33. Definition of Done

The body-tracking module is complete when:

- Gemini 2 opens automatically.
- RGB and aligned depth are available in Godot.
- MediaPipe Pose Landmarker detects up to two people.
- All 33 MediaPipe joints are available.
- Visible joints receive real Gemini-derived depth.
- Joints are converted into real XYZ coordinates.
- XYZ units are documented and consistent.
- Tracking jitter is filtered.
- Joint velocity is available.
- Two players receive reasonably persistent IDs.
- Tracking continues without blocking rendering.
- Player enter/leave events work.
- Camera disconnect does not crash Godot.
- A debug scene displays the complete tracking state.
- A normal gameplay script can use tracking without knowing about Orbbec or MediaPipe.

Target game-side usage:

```gdscript
func _process(_delta):
    var player = BodyTracker.get_player(0)

    if player == null:
        return

    var hand = player.right_hand

    $MagicOrb.global_position = camera_to_game(
        hand.position_3d
    )
```

and:

```gdscript
func _on_gesture(player, gesture):
    match gesture:
        "push":
            cast_fireball(player)
        "arms_up":
            activate_special(player)
        "crouch":
            raise_shield(player)
```

That is the abstraction level the final tracking system should provide.

