# 34. Important Engineering Rules

1. **Use Gemini depth as the authoritative physical Z coordinate.**

2. Do not treat MediaPipe's model-derived Z as equivalent to measured camera depth.

3. Align depth and RGB before looking up depth at pose landmarks.

4. Prefer median neighbourhood depth sampling instead of one-pixel sampling.

5. Keep camera SDK code out of gameplay code.

6. Keep MediaPipe landmark indices out of gameplay code.

7. Always distinguish camera coordinates from game/world coordinates.

8. Prefer low latency over processing every frame.

9. Drop stale frames rather than queueing them.

10. Profile before optimizing.

11. Keep a debug visualization available throughout development.

12. Commit after every working phase.

